  <title>4.14.4: Rules for a Sequence</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01110</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.14.4: Rules for a Sequence</md:title>
    <md:uuid>7aea918d-87ce-4049-afcf-421aa5e1601d</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down (5 minutes)</title>
<title>Student Activity</title>
<para>A sequence starts 3, 6, . . .</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> Give a rule the sequence could follow, and list the next 3 terms. </item>
  <para> <emphasis>Answer: </emphasis> Sample Responses: Each term adds 3 from the previous term. The next three terms are 9, 12, 15. </para>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> Give a different rule the sequence could follow, and list the next 3 terms. </item>
  <para> <emphasis>Answer: </emphasis> Sample Responses: Each term doubles the previous term. The next three terms are 12, 24, 48. </para>
</list>
<title>Video: Finding Rules of Sequences</title>
<para>Watch the following video to learn more about function notations.</para>
